{
"dur": 79.126,
"shots": [
{
"i": 1,
"start": 0.0,
"vo_start": 0.6,
"vo_end": 7.04,
"text": "That was the human rhythm for a very long time. Food in the morning, people in the afternoon, stories at night.",
"end": 7.315
},
{
"i": 2,
"start": 7.315,
"vo_start": 7.59,
"vo_end": 13.229,
"text": "Then, roughly twelve thousand years ago, in the Fertile Crescent, people began planting wild grains and keeping animals.",
"end": 13.504
},
{
"i": 3,
"start": 13.504,
"vo_start": 13.779,
"vo_end": 21.259,
"text": "On paper, it looked like an upgrade. More food. More control. No more tracking an antelope across the plain.",
"end": 21.534
},
{
"i": 4,
"start": 21.534,
"vo_start": 21.809,
"vo_end": 32.329,
"text": "But it set off a loop. More food meant more children survived. More people needed more food. More food meant more fields, and more fields meant more work.",
"end": 32.604
},
{
"i": 5,
"start": 32.604,
"vo_start": 32.879,
"vo_end": 38.598,
"text": "And then the door shut. Once a village grew too big to live off wild food, there was no going back.",
"end": 38.873
},
{
"i": 6,
"start": 38.873,
"vo_start": 39.148,
"vo_end": 45.114,
"text": "Ploughing, sowing, weeding, harvesting, grinding, storing and guarding. Every season, every year.",
"end": 45.389
},
{
"i": 7,
"start": 45.389,
"vo_start": 45.664,
"vo_end": 52.381,
"text": "Remember the second skeleton? The decay, the worn spine, the shorter life. This is where it came from.",
"end": 52.656
},
{
"i": 8,
"start": 52.656,
"vo_start": 52.931,
"vo_end": 62.043,
"text": "Villages became towns. Towns needed potters, weavers and traders. Then cities, and with them kings, soldiers, priests and tax collectors.",
"end": 62.318
},
{
"i": 9,
"start": 62.318,
"vo_start": 62.593,
"vo_end": 69.827,
"text": "And something new arrived in human history: hours that belonged to someone else, sold in exchange for food you no longer knew how to find.",
"end": 70.102
},
{
"i": 10,
"start": 70.102,
"vo_start": 70.377,
"vo_end": 78.176,
"text": "Nobody stole our time in one night. It was traded away slowly, over hundreds of generations, in a deal none of us got to vote on.",
"end": 79.126
}
],
